String.format("%f", 1e23) gives "100000000000000000000000.000000", as in Java 21 and 25 (Java 17 takes the digits of its Double.toString, 99999999999999990000000.000000). With --java-version 21 (Java 20 and earlier print other digits, see c6Java17 and c6Any).
(With --java-locale en-US, whose digits and case the expected string has.)
